WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.304
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B one.

2
00:00:05.604 --> 00:00:09.095
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.395 --> 00:00:15.762
Unit two: Past Continuous. Today you will describe actions in progress at a moment in the past.

4
00:00:16.062 --> 00:00:18.656
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:22.810
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:24.674
Was doing.

7
00:00:25.683 --> 00:00:29.633
Was doing means an action in progress for I, he, she and it.

8
00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:31.634
I was doing my homework.

9
00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:34.891
Your turn. Say: Was doing.

10
00:00:37.733 --> 00:00:38.792
Was doing.

11
00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:40.481
Were doing.

12
00:00:41.483 --> 00:00:44.748
Were doing means an action in progress for you, we and they.

13
00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:47.326
They were doing exercises.

14
00:00:47.917 --> 00:00:50.232
Your turn. Say: Were doing.

15
00:00:53.067 --> 00:00:54.091
Were doing.

16
00:00:54.850 --> 00:00:55.642
While.

17
00:00:56.650 --> 00:00:58.441
While means during the time that.

18
00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:00.806
I was cooking while she studied.

19
00:01:01.417 --> 00:01:03.953
Your turn. Say: While.

20
00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:07.743
While.

21
00:01:08.483 --> 00:01:09.078
When.

22
00:01:10.083 --> 00:01:11.595
When means at the time that.

23
00:01:12.183 --> 00:01:14.078
I was sleeping when you called.

24
00:01:14.683 --> 00:01:16.813
Your turn. Say: When.

25
00:01:19.667 --> 00:01:20.354
When.

26
00:01:21.117 --> 00:01:22.257
Interrupted.

27
00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:26.283
Interrupted means stopped for a short time by something.

28
00:01:26.883 --> 00:01:28.674
The call interrupted my work.

29
00:01:29.283 --> 00:01:31.854
Your turn. Say: Interrupted.

30
00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:35.852
Interrupted.

31
00:01:36.617 --> 00:01:37.966
In progress.

32
00:01:38.950 --> 00:01:41.623
In progress means happening and not yet finished.

33
00:01:42.217 --> 00:01:43.938
The work was in progress.

34
00:01:44.550 --> 00:01:47.144
Your turn. Say: In progress.

35
00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:51.431
In progress.

36
00:01:52.183 --> 00:01:53.161
Background.

37
00:01:54.150 --> 00:01:56.974
Background means the situation behind the main events.

38
00:01:57.583 --> 00:02:00.036
Rain was the background of the story.

39
00:02:00.650 --> 00:02:03.209
Your turn. Say: Background.

40
00:02:06.067 --> 00:02:07.056
Background.

41
00:02:07.817 --> 00:02:08.632
Ongoing.

42
00:02:09.617 --> 00:02:12.092
Ongoing means continuing without stopping.

43
00:02:12.683 --> 00:02:14.416
It was an ongoing project.

44
00:02:15.017 --> 00:02:17.425
Your turn. Say: Ongoing.

45
00:02:20.267 --> 00:02:21.349
Ongoing.

46
00:02:22.133 --> 00:02:25.633
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:26.483 --> 00:02:29.435
Visal, what were you doing yesterday at eight o'clock?

48
00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:42.075
I was having dinner. The past continuous is was or were plus the -ing form. It describes an action in progress at a particular moment in the past.

49
00:02:43.183 --> 00:02:45.125
How is it used with the past simple?

50
00:02:46.217 --> 00:02:57.179
The past continuous is the longer background action and the past simple is the short action that interrupts it: I was reading when the phone rang.

51
00:02:58.283 --> 00:02:59.342
And while?

52
00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:12.590
While joins two long actions: I was cooking while my brother was studying. When is common with a short action. Notice that state verbs like know or want are not used in the continuous.

53
00:03:13.733 --> 00:03:15.118
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:15.983 --> 00:03:20.572
Grammar focus: Past continuous: was and were plus verb-ing.

55
00:03:20.872 --> 00:03:22.024
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:22.717 --> 00:03:24.763
I was having dinner at eight o'clock.

57
00:03:25.650 --> 00:03:27.452
I was reading when the phone rang.

58
00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:30.245
She was cooking while he was studying.

59
00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:40.110
Use was / were + verb-ing for the background action in progress, and the past simple for the short action that interrupts. While joins two long actions.

60
00:03:40.850 --> 00:03:44.536
Be careful! Don't say: I was knowing the answer.

61
00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:48.151
Say: I knew the answer.

62
00:03:48.451 --> 00:03:50.323
Do not use know in the continuous.

63
00:03:51.133 --> 00:03:53.890
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:54.700 --> 00:03:56.247
In the Middle of Things.

65
00:03:56.547 --> 00:03:59.754
Yesterday at eight o'clock I was having dinner with my family.

66
00:04:00.767 --> 00:04:03.904
While my mother was cooking, my father was reading the news.

67
00:04:04.900 --> 00:04:06.992
I was studying when my friend called.

68
00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:11.091
It was raining, so the children were playing inside.

69
00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:14.576
The ongoing rain was the background of the whole day.

70
00:04:15.667 --> 00:04:19.634
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:20.483 --> 00:04:22.402
I blank TV when she called.

72
00:04:22.702 --> 00:04:26.436
A, watched. B, was watching. C, am watching.

73
00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:32.069
The answer is B: was watching.

74
00:04:33.217 --> 00:04:34.984
They blank football at five.

75
00:04:35.284 --> 00:04:38.763
A, was playing. B, were playing. C, played.

76
00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:44.636
The answer is B: were playing.

77
00:04:45.783 --> 00:04:48.970
She cooked blank he studied. (two long actions)

78
00:04:49.270 --> 00:04:51.936
A, when. B, while. C, then.

79
00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:57.174
The answer is B: while.

80
00:04:58.317 --> 00:04:59.933
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:05:00.233 --> 00:05:05.524
A, I was knowing the answer.. B, I knew the answer.. C, I was know the answer..

82
00:05:09.067 --> 00:05:11.693
The answer is B: I knew the answer..

83
00:05:12.850 --> 00:05:15.418
According to the reading, who was reading the news?

84
00:05:15.718 --> 00:05:19.488
A, the father. B, the mother. C, the friend.

85
00:05:23.033 --> 00:05:25.312
The answer is A: the father.

86
00:05:26.500 --> 00:05:29.802
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:30.650 --> 00:05:32.963
What were you doing yesterday at 8pm?

88
00:05:41.750 --> 00:05:43.285
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:43.585 --> 00:05:57.864
Yesterday at eight o'clock I was doing my homework. My mother was cooking in the kitchen, and my brother was watching TV. Suddenly the lights went out. I use the past continuous for the background and the past simple for the interruption.

90
00:05:58.164 --> 00:05:59.897
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:00.783 --> 00:06:06.559
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and past continuous: was and were plus verb-ing.

92
00:06:06.859 --> 00:06:10.858
Today's value is reflection. Think about what you learned and how you grew.

93
00:06:11.158 --> 00:06:13.706
See you in Unit three. Goodbye!

94
00:06:14.006 --> 00:06:17.006
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

